<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
	Per-class combat playstyles for recruited phantom party members.
	Loaded at boot; reload live with //phantom playstyle.

	A <playstyle> covers a class LINEAGE. `classIds` lists every PlayerClass id it applies to; a member
	resolves by its EXACT class id, and skills it hasn't learned are skipped at runtime - so one entry can
	span a whole career. Document order = priority: each tick the engine casts the FIRST entry whose
	conditions pass. A skill the class knows but this file does not list is deliberately never used.

	`role` (optional) disambiguates lineages whose CLASS is shared between two archetypes: a level 20-39
	Human archer and dagger are both a plain Rogue (id 7), so class id alone can't tell them apart. A
	role-specific playstyle wins over a role-agnostic one. Valid roles are the party roles:
	TANK, WARRIOR, ARCHER, DAGGER, MONK, SINGER, DANCER, NUKER.

	<skill> attributes:
	  id           - skill id (level resolved from what the member learned)
	  name         - documentation only (the id is authoritative)
	  use          - OPENER | ROTATION | AOE | DEBUFF | CONTROL | PANIC | LIMIT | PULL | STANCE
	                 (PANIC/LIMIT target self; LIMIT additionally needs a ready healer)
	                 STANCE is a combat toggle (Vicious Stance): turned on in a fight while it is off, and turned off
	                 again once the member is out of combat, so it does not drain MP while resting.
	                 PULL is special: it is the ranged opener the CAMP PULLER uses to tag a mob (so a nuker
	                 shoots it instead of running in to body-pull) and is read ONLY by the pull hook, never by
	                 the combat rotation. Use a cheap single-target nuke. Its `when` is ignored - the pull hook
	                 supplies its own gating (in cast range, and above the role's MP reserve). TANKS pull with
	                 Aggression, which is manager-owned and handled in code, so it is NOT listed here.
	  when         - comma-separated AND conditions:
	                 ALWAYS, TARGET_HP_BELOW (hpBelow), TARGET_HP_ABOVE (hpAbove),
	                 SELF_HP_BELOW (selfHpBelow), MP_ABOVE (mpAbove), MOBS_NEAR (mobsAtLeast),
	                 MOBS_UNSPOILED (mobsAtLeast), REAR, CHARGES (chargesAtLeast), CHARGES_BELOW (chargesBelow),
	                 DEBUFF_MISSING, SELF_ABNORMAL_FREE, NOT_SPOILED, DURABLE_TARGET, HEALER_READY,
	                 ONCE_PER_TARGET, UNDER_ATTACK, PVP (the target is a player), FOCUS_ON_ME (the target has
	                 this member selected)
	  minLevel/maxLevel - the level window this entry applies in. Unlearned skills are skipped anyway, so
	                 minLevel is rarely needed; maxLevel is what RETIRES an outgrown skill (a level 80
	                 archer still knows Power Shot, so only an explicit cap stops it being used).
	  paceMs       - optional per-entry pacing floor (engine default ~1.6-2.5s between casts)

	Mechanics (cast range, MP, reuse, reagents, weapon requirements, cast-time HP gates like Frenzy's)
	come from the skill data at runtime and are never written here. Listing a skill the member can't
	currently cast is harmless - it is simply skipped.

	Unlisted skills: when nothing listed fits a tick, the engine may cast the best of the member's own unlisted
	single-target attack or debuff skills (PhantomSkillFallback in FakePlayers.ini; never dances, songs, toggles,
	heals, buffs, area skills, taunts, Sleep, Root or Spoil). Listing a skill hands it to this file: to keep an
	outgrown skill from coming back through the fallback, list it with a maxLevel. HEALER_READY is always open to a
	solo phantom (a field hunter or an Olympiad noble), which has no party healer to wait for.

	FAIL-SAFE: if a member knows NONE of its playstyle's level-applicable skills, the engine does not take
	over at all and the member keeps stock auto-use behavior. This system can only add competence.

	NOT covered on purpose:
	- Support classes (Cleric/Bishop/Cardinal, Prophet/Hierophant, Elven Elder/Eva's Saint, Shillien
	  Elder/Shillien Saint, Overlord/Dominator, Warcryer/Doomcryer): their combat behavior is the party
	  manager's support tick (heals/buffs/recharge/cleanse/res), which already plays the class.
	- Summoner lineages (Warlock/Arcana Lord, Elemental Summoner/Elemental Master, Phantom
	  Summoner/Spectral Master): servitor control is a later phase.
	- Manager-owned skills - NEVER list these: Ultimate Defense (110), Aggression (28), Aura of Hate (18),
	  Sleep (1069), Dryad Root (1201), Resurrection (1016), heals, songs and dances. The party manager
	  casts them with its own threat/survival/CC/support logic.
	- Toggles and stances (Arcane Power, Parry Stance...): only toggles listed with use="STANCE" are ever
	  turned on (so far the daggers' Vicious Stance); the rest are still unused (FPC-133).
	- Spoil/Sweeper (loot integration) and cubic upkeep (needs a "cubic missing" condition).
-->
<list xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="xsd/PhantomPlaystyles.xsd">

	<!-- =====================================================================================
	     BASE STARTING CLASSES (levels 1-19, BEFORE the 1st class transfer). These are the nine
	     race-and-type root classes a character wears until its 1st transfer (~level 20), after
	     which its class id changes and one of the entries further down takes over. A recruited
	     member is level-matched to the player, so a low-level party is built from these ids -
	     without an entry here an early-game phantom kept stock auto-attack and never used a skill.

	     The kit at this tier is tiny (a base class learns its first real skills at level 5-7 and
	     has only a handful before transfer) - so, as elsewhere, that handful IS the playstyle.
	     Heals, self/party buff toggles and the manager-owned CC list stay out (same rules as the
	     rest of this file); what remains is the class's actual offensive/utility skills. Members
	     below the learn level simply know none of these and fall back to stock behavior (fail-safe).
	     ===================================================================================== -->

	<!-- Human Fighter (0) -> every human fighter career. Weapon-agnostic like the Warrior generic:
	     the bow/dagger/blunt hit each fail their weapon check unless the rolled weapon fits, so only
	     the matching one fires. -->
	<playstyle name="Human Fighter (base)" classIds="0">
		<skill id="56" name="Power Shot"   use="ROTATION" when="MP_ABOVE" mpAbove="40" paceMs="4000" />
		<skill id="16" name="Mortal Blow"  use="ROTATION" when="MP_ABOVE" mpAbove="30" />
		<skill id="3"  name="Power Strike" use="ROTATION" when="MP_ABOVE" mpAbove="40" />
	</playstyle>

	<!-- Elven Fighter (18) -> temple knight / swordsinger / scout lines. Same three-weapon spread;
	     its auras (77/91) and Elemental Heal are toggles/self-heal and stay manager/upkeep-owned. -->
	<playstyle name="Elven Fighter (base)" classIds="18">
		<skill id="56" name="Power Shot"   use="ROTATION" when="MP_ABOVE" mpAbove="40" paceMs="4000" />
		<skill id="16" name="Mortal Blow"  use="ROTATION" when="MP_ABOVE" mpAbove="30" />
		<skill id="3"  name="Power Strike" use="ROTATION" when="MP_ABOVE" mpAbove="40" />
	</playstyle>

	<!-- Dark Fighter (31) -> palus knight / assassin lines. Adds Drain Health for sustain. -->
	<playstyle name="Dark Fighter (base)" classIds="31">
		<skill id="56" name="Power Shot"   use="ROTATION" when="MP_ABOVE" mpAbove="40" paceMs="4000" />
		<skill id="16" name="Mortal Blow"  use="ROTATION" when="MP_ABOVE" mpAbove="30" />
		<skill id="70" name="Drain Health" use="ROTATION" when="MP_ABOVE" mpAbove="40" />
		<skill id="3"  name="Power Strike" use="ROTATION" when="MP_ABOVE" mpAbove="45" />
	</playstyle>

	<!-- Orc Fighter (44) -> raider/destroyer + monk/tyrant lines. Fists and blunt. -->
	<playstyle name="Orc Fighter (base)" classIds="44">
		<skill id="29" name="Iron Punch"   use="ROTATION" when="MP_ABOVE" mpAbove="40" />
		<skill id="3"  name="Power Strike" use="ROTATION" when="MP_ABOVE" mpAbove="45" />
	</playstyle>

	<!-- Dwarven Fighter (53) -> scavenger/bounty hunter + artisan/warsmith. No attack skills at base;
	     its one combat-relevant early skill is Spoil (learned at 10) - same NOT_SPOILED handling as
	     the Dwarf 2nd classes. Below 10 it knows nothing here and just auto-attacks. -->
	<playstyle name="Dwarven Fighter (base)" classIds="53">
		<skill id="254" name="Spoil" use="DEBUFF" when="NOT_SPOILED" />
	</playstyle>

